about: a value is found in an expanded array by its JSON-escaped form, so a backslash or quote in it still matches
op: deleteJsonValueAt
path: ["patterns"]
literal: "a\\ b\"c"
=== input
{
  "patterns": [
    "plain",
    "a\\ b\"c",
    "last"
  ]
}
=== output
{
  "patterns": [
    "plain",
    "last"
  ]
}
=== at
1
